  "reviewerNote": "Real halftone scene from a 1908 chromolithograph: every place name is lettered directly on the printed screen (pitch 6 px at this scan's 451 DPI, unchanged by the app because the image is far above the upscale floor). The letterforms are outline-drawn and follow the drapery and the map's perspective, so these are region-level boxes over rotated lettering - the proxy the strategic spec allows - not glyph-tight masks. MONTENEGRO is marked partly-illegible: it is small, faint and set into a fold. Geometry placed by eye against a 100 px coordinate grid (temp/ocrscreen/view grid); no OCR was involved.",
